      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_805e1c28a9a11b89377a66355295af9626b94637700c6d35d7815c5a9b9ea6de",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "A smoothed threshold kernel and multidimensional contour inversion convert controlled Fourier-Laplace transforms on the required contour range into precise one-point Gaussian tail products. For separated points, the covariance cross terms are explicitly negligible on those contours, leaving two copies of the one-point Gaussian integral and hence asymptotic factorization.",
